+# gets a required, indexed account_id.
+#
+# Rows are backfilled from their parent record. Rows whose account can't be
+# resolved, or whose account no longer exists, are orphans and are deleted.
+#
+# Tables are processed parents-first so that orphans cascade: a card dropped
+# for lacking an account leaves its comments without a parent to backfill
+# from, so they're dropped too.
